2026-10-18T01:04:18.8507814Z -- #369/#370/#1738 — the duplication window can fire, and --record refuses a laundered regression
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8508077Z   ok   a copy in ANOTHER module is one copy, whatever its locals are called (#1738 a)
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8508287Z   ok   a third copy costs one more, not two more: copies, not pairs
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8509010Z   ok   a re-wrap or a comment moves nothing: the window is the AST, not the lines
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8509244Z   ok   the node floor holds: two short shared statements are not a copy
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8509470Z   ok   the shipped window is 2 statements of at least 30 nodes (#1738)
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8509742Z   ok   regression_rows names the metric that moved the wrong way, old and new (#370)
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8510016Z   ok   cross_seam_edges moving up IS a regression row: the retired ratio's band is gone
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8510281Z   ok   --record REFUSES a worsened metric by default and leaves the table untouched
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8510562Z   ok   an explicit --allow-regression reason lets it through and writes the new value
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8510822Z   ok   a blank reason is refused, so the flag cannot decay into pasted boilerplate
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8511101Z   ok   a pure tightening still records with no flag -- that is the point of the exercise
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8511350Z   ok   and the path that proceeds still stamps a resolvable recorded_at (#363)
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8511706Z   ok   cross_seam_edges is recorded like every other row -- a tightening lands
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8511949Z   ok   --allow-regression is a flag that demands a reason, not a bare switch
2026-10-18T01:04:18.8511959Z 
